course: dictionary
lesson: 12665
title: Dissolved: mixed in, broken up, or overcome
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Dissolved» comes from the verb «dissolve». When a solid like sugar dissolves in a liquid like water, it breaks into pieces so tiny you cannot see them, and it mixes evenly through the liquid. «I stirred the sugar, and it dissolved in my tea.» You can't see the sugar any more, but it is still there, which is why the tea tastes sweet.
explain: Dissolved can also mean ended or broken up. «The club was dissolved after the last meeting.» Nobody is mixed into anything here. The club has stopped existing as a group. Check the other words in the sentence to find which meaning fits.
explain: In a story, dissolved can describe a feeling. «The class dissolved into giggles when the teacher slipped on the wet floor.» The children did not melt or mix into anything. They suddenly started laughing so much they could not stop. Ask yourself: what would the sentence mean if I swapped in a simple word like «laughed a lot»?
fact: Dissolve means to mix completely into a liquid so the solid cannot be seen any more.
fact: Salt and sugar dissolve in water, but sand does not.
fact: Stirring and warm water help things dissolve faster.
fact: «Dissolved oxygen» is oxygen mixed into water, and fish breathe it.
fact: «Dissolved into tears» or «dissolved into laughter» means started crying or laughing a lot, all at once.
exercise: «Stir the sugar, and it dissolves in the tea.» What does dissolves mean? | Gets hot and starts to burn | Turns into a gas and disappears into the air | Floats on top in lumps | *Mixes completely into the liquid so you cannot see it
exercise: Priya says, «The salt has dissolved, so I can't see it any more.» Where is the salt now? | *Still in the water, mixed in tiny pieces | Gone out of the room | Turned into sand | Lying at the bottom as a heap
exercise: «The class dissolved into giggles.» What does dissolved into giggles mean? | Suddenly started crying | Ended and went home early | *Suddenly started laughing a lot | Fell fast asleep
test: «Sand does not dissolve in water; it just sinks to the bottom.» Which one would dissolve in warm water? | *Sugar | Pebbles | Gravel | Sand
test: «The club was dissolved after the last meeting.» What does dissolved mean here? | Mixed into a drink | Started crying | *Ended or broken up | Made very warm
exam: Ben says his sugar dissolved faster in the hot tea than in the cold tea. What helps things dissolve faster? | Putting the lid on tight | *Warm water and stirring | Using a cold, still liquid | Waiting for the sugar to float
